 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch washer FD 9409 not draining. ive cleaned the filter already. what part do i need?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I cannot tell you which part to buy yet because 'not draining' after cleaning the filter usually points to one of two different faults: either the drain hose/waste pipe is blocked further down, or the pump itself has failed (or something is jammed in it). To separate these, please run a drain or spin-only programme and listen carefully near the bottom front of the machine while it tries to empty. Do you hear the pump humming or buzzing as it works, or is there total silence?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "It hums but the water doesn't move. Loud hum with a bit of a rattle. So is it the pump then?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drain pump]\nBecause I cannot verify the exact internal layout for model FD 9409 in my database, I cannot guarantee part compatibility from a generic search. You should purchase a drain pump specifically listed for your Bosch model number (check the rating plate on the door frame or side of the machine) and replace it yourself if you are comfortable with basic DIY, or contact an engineer to do so."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The FD 9409 is off the sticker inside the door, the E-Nr line next to it is rubbed off so I can't read the full model number. Front just says Bosch Serie 4 and VarioPerfect. Is that enough to order a pump or not?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "AI service unavailable. Please try again in a moment."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Your reply just says 'AI service unavailable'. Can you try again? Is the FD 9409 plus Bosch Serie 4 VarioPerfect enough to order a pump, or not?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drain pump]\nNo, that information is not enough to order the correct part safely. The 'FD 9409' is likely just a series or marketing code; Bosch parts require the full E-Nr (Electrical Number) found on the rating plate to ensure compatibility. Given that you hear a loud hum with a rattle but no water moves, the drain pump has almost certainly failed (likely a jammed impeller or burnt motor). Because you cannot get the full model number to verify the part, and replacing this component involves disconnecting electrical connectors and managing water spillage during removal, I recommend calling an engineer. They will have the tools to identify the exact pump needed from the machine's serial data and can replace it safely."
  }
 ],
